= Public-input q0 lowering diagnostic source checkpoint

This auxiliary archive preserves the completed private adaptation of the tracked
qcd-ladder ignored test, its compile and guarded-execution control sources, and
the source/settings audit. It does not replace production code or add a public
API. See #raw("vakint-5l-public-q0-lowering-source-20261026.tar.gz") and
#raw("public_q0_lowering_checkpoint.json"). All twenty members are source or
small source-provenance records; the imported Rust admission module and the
Python actor, parent-admission, policy and guard sources are included.

The base is Main #raw("03ad1ecfd75b776723562ab2a17e1393b17ccd84"), with
RustRed #raw("4190f2c6f3158e3fc3cbcb1937e12e5971da9175") and official
Symbolica #raw("9cd57678d8817ec33c05cacba4925162f1c86b0b"). The private
source snapshot is #raw("bfe0dc784735c3d7604782afe8a068e71fe0bfc9e70ae3c1478dda4372cf45bb"),
and the adapted diagnostic source is
#raw("adbdbe03ae093ae63a3bf4ccc00b9658711385f1f7d7c02973707bacad05336b").
Those identities describe different layers. Rebuilding the private test produced
different RLIB bytes from historical builds; equal revisions are not a claim of
binary identity or equivalent performance.

The test reuses authenticated prepared scalar input through the actual public
canonicalization, tensor, matching, replacement, scalar-lowering and mass-channel
sequence, stopping before IBP. It retains every contribution and request batch,
including raw inputs outside recorded coverage. Prepared-cache loading is off;
one fresh engine performs ordinary activation and its existing settings reload.
The source expects two snapshot preparations, without claiming an observed
import counter. The diagnostic owner inspection is Advisory and preserves the
original matching predicate. No master coefficients or campaign certification
are changed.

The enclosed audit compares the frozen active producer with this private source.
Both explicitly enable dot notation and disable prepared-cache loading. All 21
settings defaults match, and relevant overrides and mathematical methods are
accounted for. The Native comparison finds 2,700 identical Rust files, a sole
excluded test-fixture change, and 18 identical Cargo manifests. Passive test,
Python and monitoring differences are localized. The source relationship plus a
separately validated replay can support an inferred active-input inventory; it
is not direct instrumentation of the running worker. Historical 1,659-root
explicit-witness diagnostics remain separate from the public-path census.

The archive contains no ELF, RLIB, build tree, scientific input, census, trace,
cache, license value, environment file, active configuration, launch specification,
registration ticket or runtime result. Original absolute development paths and
expected hashes in the control sources are historical facts. Extraction grants
no authority to start Native work. Check out the stated base, apply the patch and
copy both overlay sources only in a new private workspace; regenerate source and
build identities, authenticate the actual libraries, and obtain fresh resource
admission before any execution. Never reuse archived hashes after relocation or
modification as a new build attestation.

Two archive passes are byte-identical, regular member paths and checksums were
verified, Python source was parsed without imports, Rust formatting and shell
syntax were checked, and this Typst note was compiled. No full CI, portable
fresh-host rebuild, final-release acceptance or new benchmark comparison is
claimed by this packaging. The separate new-suite design is still a proposal
and is intentionally excluded from this checkpoint.
